n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nA first-order linear differential equation is inhomogeneous if it is not homogeneous, i.e., if it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $Q$ is not identical to zero.\n\nTo determine which equations are inhomogeneous, we examine each one in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=-2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)=-2$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=y.\n$$\n\nWe collect the $y$-terms on the left side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y & =y \\\\ {y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y-y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+({x}^{2}-1)y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$  Therefore, this equation *is* homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=-2$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eea5aa8-c67d-5ad3-911c-0f9b71c1f33e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670812} {:answer/id #uuid "95d22fdd-50a8-58bc-ba28-8ea3cc513275" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95d22fdd-50a8-58bc-ba28-8ea3cc513275" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670824} :answer-field/id #uuid "a916be7d-2c5c-5232-b92b-9d597b7061e7" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+4xy={x}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "062d8748-bc07-5aa6-9588-2b82d547067c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670798} {:answer/id #uuid "c12ed845-7c03-5f67-804f-523fa748afa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c12ed845-7c03-5f67-804f-523fa748afa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670829} :answer-field/id #uuid "c970d060-b960-5030-b61d-6b1ddad40818" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+4xy=3x$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a45a63b-566f-5c4c-940b-0a8f8df66a60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670804} {:answer/id #uuid "2d6fd131-4d4b-5c1d-87bc-fd9d9eee9504" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d6fd131-4d4b-5c1d-87bc-fd9d9eee9504" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670808} :answer-field/id #uuid "df3928d3-9553-5b66-b88b-336095f3c563" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+4xy=2y$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670843}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32e86b1c-ca7c-583b-acda-148bc8829f40" :question/problem "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy=2y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+4xy & =2y \\\\ {y}^{′}+4xy-2y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(4x-2)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy=3x.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)=3x$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy={x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)={x}^{3}$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}+4xy=2y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce96936f-8d93-5d74-84f7-cba7f5c9d74b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670834} {:answer/id #uuid "e7142a29-9310-5bc9-9b7b-532824bb0e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7142a29-9310-5bc9-9b7b-532824bb0e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670844} :answer-field/id #uuid "33b0716a-3a08-565d-ab4d-7ef439c1f8bd" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670810} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "687d2052-ac77-5d7c-a136-f6f8c22b92d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670818} {:answer/id #uuid "9cde3418-92ae-5e09-8723-e8ae6a876edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "687d2052-ac77-5d7c-a136-f6f8c22b92d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670818} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c1d467f-a28a-579f-bc4b-7a801f7e6849" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=-2y$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e9dea5-b7d0-57c3-9af6-d37ced5b1167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670800} {:answer/id #uuid "c959746e-3371-5185-af4b-5cb2e865cf30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c959746e-3371-5185-af4b-5cb2e865cf30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670832} :answer-field/id #uuid "da2b1882-93e1-5f9f-b4e8-6d22449e2db3" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670842}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f661f26-2894-5b15-9e23-c052d8e0ebda" :question/problem "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=2.\n$$\n\nThe presence of the constant term $2$ means the right-hand side is not zero, and so it cannot be rewritten in homogeneous form. Thus, this equation is *not* homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=-2y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y & =-2y \\\\ {y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y+2y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+({x}^{3}+2)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=0$; ${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=-2y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670823 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59ec5fa-9d13-5fc4-8c6d-4334df2e5574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670837} {:answer/id #uuid "f9763a24-d037-571b-9f03-46dc3f319384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9763a24-d037-571b-9f03-46dc3f319384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670846} :answer-field/id #uuid "552f7559-74ed-50e1-8505-9c756f346ad2" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670814} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95337301-0306-5473-a840-a3665a504b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670822} {:answer/id #uuid "c27b9007-5b5b-5a6f-b4cf-fe3bd9a381dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95337301-0306-5473-a840-a3665a504b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670822} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf285f5d-b22c-5312-bf34-858cc56e87cb" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=-5y$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670828} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "362509b0-7f13-5268-9882-b7458181febd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670811} {:answer/id #uuid "d330c53d-36a0-5743-9be6-dd2c47e5129a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "362509b0-7f13-5268-9882-b7458181febd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670811} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9234d2f-f7ae-5ff4-b1cf-c005b486a2de" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=4y$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670840}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95870580-b5cf-5914-9a93-1e8255bc81ca" :question/problem "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=4y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y & =4y \\\\ {y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y-4y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(8{x}^{3}-4)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=-5y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y & =-5y \\\\ {y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y+5y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(8{x}^{3}+5)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=-3.\n$$\n\nThe presence of the constant term $-3$ means the right-hand side is not zero, and so it cannot be rewritten in homogeneous form. Thus, this equation is *not* homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=4y$; ${y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=-5y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a514407-d3f3-575f-b9fa-d8b32140637f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true